This is not recommended and will make your site vunerable, link your instance to a proper server with no access. This is temporary and will have loopholes

Login Requirement: 0 - None, 1 - Username & Password & 2 - Pin
Login Browser Cache: 0 - Dont cache the login in the browser 1 - Do cache the login in the browser

*START_READ*

redirected=false
redirect_url=null

login_requirement=1
username=default
password=0000
pin=null

block_paths=[/admin/,/temporary/]

login_browser_cache=1

firmware=v0.1.1
app_name=Raid for SnipeHub

*STOP_READ*

As we have said, Raid is a temporary fix. Use a proper server to store credentials so no users can access the admin and temporary files.

To redirect the read to your server, edit redirected=false to redirected=true and change the redirect_url from null to the url or IP.
